Build, installation and rollback
================================

Target: Nvidia Tegra MHI2_ER_AUG22_K3344 / MU1438, classic Virtual Cockpit.
Use a parked vehicle, stable power, known-good backups and existing SSH or
M.I.B. access. Scripts do not reboot the MMI or install an SSH server.

1. Build prerequisites
----------------------
Python 3, a host C compiler, a current JDK and Docker are required.
The HMI build uses Java 8 in eclipse-temurin:8-jdk-jammy.
Native builds use the local Docker image mhi2-qnx65-armv7-public:4.9.

Toolchain setup:
    https://github.com/luka-dev/qnx65-armv7-toolchain
    Reference commit: 56a66557245af14077678cd28a83ce3a337d9e2d

In that toolchain checkout, after supplying its required SDK inputs:
    docker buildx build --platform=linux/amd64 --target base-env \
      --build-arg BASE=base-4.9 --load -t mhi2-qnx65-armv7-public:4.9 .

2. Firmware build inputs
------------------------
Download the published MU1438 input archive and verify every file:
    python3 scripts/fetch-firmware.py

This step requires GitHub CLI (gh). Alternatively, download the archive from:
    https://github.com/aberbic/Audi-MHI2-Virtual-Cockpit-Altscreen-CarPlay-AndroidAuto/releases/tag/mu1438-build-inputs-20261003
Then verify/install it with:
    python3 scripts/fetch-firmware.py --archive /path/to/mu1438-build-inputs.tar.gz

The helper checks archive/member hashes and never overwrites differing inputs.
The archive provides these files in inputs/:

    dio_manager.stock   /mnt/app/eso/bin/apps/dio_manager
    gal.stock           /mnt/app/eso/bin/apps/gal
    gal.json.stock      /mnt/system/etc/eso/production/gal.json
    lsd.jxe             /ifs/lsd.jxe
    mu1438-stock.jar    Already converted from that exact lsd.jxe

To supply your own originals instead, use the same filenames. Conversion tool:
    https://github.com/luka-dev/jxe2jar
    Reference commit: 9eeb45bbf14bf8afe3452c7be96a4d1f0206a286

Also place these dependencies in inputs/:
    asm-9.7.jar
    asm-tree-9.7.jar
    org.osgi.framework-1.10.0.jar

Firmware fingerprints are in profiles/mu1438.json and the release manifest is
firmware/mu1438-inputs.json. Do not substitute patched live copies or bypass a
mismatch. inputs/ and generated bundles stay Git-ignored. No complete flash
image is needed; the release contains only the five listed build inputs.

3. Prepare the install bundle
-----------------------------
From this repository:
    bash scripts/test.sh
    bash scripts/build-hmi.sh
    bash scripts/build-tools.sh
    python3 scripts/prepare-bundle.py

Outputs:
    out/bundle/         SSH payload
    out/mib-sd/mod/     M.I.B. SD-card module

Move an existing bundle/SD output aside before rebuilding. Packaging uses the
tested native binaries in bin/. Rebuilds stay in component out/ directories;
developer replacements require separate validation and artifact-hash updates.

The AA renderer, hook and generated gal.json are a matched set. The only
configuration change is supportedFrameRates [30, 60] to [30]. Do not omit it.

4. Install over SSH
-------------------
Configure an SSH alias outside the repository; examples use "mib". Disconnect
both projection phones and wait for their processes to exit, then run:

    bash scripts/install-ssh.sh --check mib
    bash scripts/install-ssh.sh --install mib

The installer verifies all ten payloads, saves prior files, stages replacements
and verifies them after publication. It returns /mnt/app and /mnt/system to
read-only. Save the printed backup directory and copy it to your computer.
Restart MMI manually while parked, then reconnect one phone.

5. Install through M.I.B.
------------------------
Use an existing M.I.B. More Incredible Bash SD setup:
    https://github.com/Mr-MIBonk/M.I.B._More-Incredible-Bash

Back up any existing mod/custom.sh and mod/command.sh on the card. Copy the
contents of out/mib-sd/ onto it. Run the custom/individual script from M.I.B.
Advanced Settings with both phones disconnected. Retain the printed backup
path, then restart MMI manually. Do not use the red SWDL firmware-update menu.

6. Check and restore
--------------------
Before driving, check centre-screen rotary/select/back input, cluster takeover,
guidance stop/start, disconnect/reconnect, and native-map restoration. Verify
normal gauges and warnings remain available. AA wheel zoom is not supported.

To restore, disconnect both phones and use the exact printed backup path:
    ssh mib '/bin/sh /mnt/app/root/altscreen-backups/BACKUP/altscreen-install.sh --restore --parked'

Replace BACKUP with your saved directory name. This restores the prior state,
not necessarily factory state; newly added files are retained in the backup.
Unexpected later changes stop rollback. Restart MMI manually afterward.

Touchpad and navigation metadata are unfinished and excluded by default.
Do not install experimental metadata artifacts as a working release.
